# Build-context pruning for tests/stress/docker/Dockerfile.
#
# This file has to sit at the *build context root*, which is the repository
# root: the `docker build` in scripts/stress-docker.js, the compose file's
# `context: ../../..` and the CI workflow all pass `.` as the context. Docker's
# classic builder reads `.dockerignore` from there and nowhere else; only
# BuildKit also honours a `<Dockerfile>.dockerignore` next to the Dockerfile,
# and a buildx plugin is not installed everywhere (this repo's own machines
# fall back to the classic builder, which would then ship the full 2.3 GB).
#
# Without this file every build ships ~2.3 GB to the daemon before the first
# layer runs: .git (1.3 GB), the root node_modules (320 MB) and the
# devtools-frontend submodule (655 MB).
#
# The image copies only `package.json`, `package-lock.json` and `build/` - the
# host compiles the suite (see the Dockerfile header), so the source trees stay
# out of the context entirely.
.git
**/.git
.idea
.github
docs
skills
*.log
stress-run.log

# Root install only; the image runs its own `npm ci`.
node_modules

# Not copied: the image ships compiled output. Keeping this excluded is what
# keeps the context at ~35 MB instead of ~490 MB.
third_party

# Not copied either: the tests and their helpers are already compiled into
# build/tests/**, which `npm run build` regenerates before the image is built.
src
tests
scripts